        {
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 7.28,
          "text": "We just derived this relation here."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.28,
          "end": 10.08,
          "text": "The relation between the differential of the speed of"
        },
        {
          "start": 10.08,
          "end": 13.24,
          "text": "the rocket's lead and the differential of the mass of"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.24,
          "end": 14.44,
          "text": "the rocket."
        },
        {
          "start": 14.44,
          "end": 17.76,
          "text": "And we want to ultimately get the speed of the rocket."
        },
        {
          "start": 17.76,
          "end": 21.64,
          "text": "So we have to apply a technique called separation"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.64,
          "end": 23.0,
          "text": "variables."
        },
        {
          "start": 23.0,
          "end": 25.96,
          "text": "And then we want to integrate."
        },
        {
          "start": 25.96,
          "end": 29.8,
          "text": "What we're going to do is, first, we're going to"
        },
        {
          "start": 29.8,
          "end": 33.32,
          "text": "multiply by dt, so that falls away."
        },
        {
          "start": 33.32,
          "end": 42.32,
          "text": "And we're left with mR dvR equals dmRu."
        },
        {
          "start": 42.32,
          "end": 47.0,
          "text": "And we're going to shuffle the m onto the other side."
        },
        {
          "start": 47.0,
          "end": 51.16,
          "text": "And we're left with dvR equals u is a constant."
        },
        {
          "start": 51.16,
          "end": 53.24,
          "text": "So that goes up front."
        },
        {
          "start": 53.24,
          "end": 58.56,
          "text": "And then we have dmR over mR."
        },
        {
          "start": 58.56,
          "end": 61.68,
          "text": "That's an equation that we can integrate now."
        },
        {
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 65.76,
          "text": "And we can do that."
        },
        {
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 69.2,
          "text": "And the tricky bit is that we need to take care of the"
        },
        {
          "start": 69.2,
          "end": 70.96,
          "text": "integration limits here."
        },
        {
          "start": 70.96,
          "end": 76.4,
          "text": "We have vR, and actually these now are all primes."
        },
        {
          "start": 76.4,
          "end": 80.84,
          "text": "So we have vR going from v0."
        },
        {
          "start": 80.84,
          "end": 83.48,
          "text": "That is our initial condition here."
        },
        {
          "start": 83.48,
          "end": 94.12,
          "text": "2 vR prime of t."
        },
        {
          "start": 94.12,
          "end": 99.32,
          "text": "And for the mass, we have mR prime equals m0."
        },
        {
          "start": 99.32,
          "end": 100.8,
          "text": "Actually, not quite m0."
        },
        {
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 107.76,
          "text": "It's 2 m0, because the initial mass of this is the dry mass"
        },
        {
          "start": 107.76,
          "end": 108.68,
          "text": "and the fuel mass."
        },
        {
          "start": 108.68,
          "end": 111.6,
          "text": "So that's 2 m0."
        },
        {
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 116.4,
          "text": "So this is the initial mass."
        },
        {
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 124.92,
          "text": "And then we go to mR prime equals m of vR."
        },
        {
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 127.4,
          "text": "All right, so let's do that."
        },
        {
          "start": 127.4,
          "end": 136.96,
          "text": "We're going to get vR minus v0 equals u1 over m."
        },
        {
          "start": 136.96,
          "end": 139.56,
          "text": "Integrated gives us an ln."
        },
        {
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 141.32,
          "text": "So ln."
        },
        {
          "start": 141.32,
          "end": 152.81,
          "text": "And then we can immediately do this here over 2 m0."
        },
        {
          "start": 152.81,
          "end": 156.89,
          "text": "And we ultimately want this."
        },
        {
          "start": 156.89,
          "end": 159.01,
          "text": "So this is a vR of t, of course."
        },
        {
          "start": 159.01,
          "end": 171.65,
          "text": "And then we got v0 plus u ln mR over 2 m0."
        },
        {
          "start": 171.65,
          "end": 176.78,
          "text": "And that is our equation."
        },
        {
          "start": 176.78,
          "end": 179.58,
          "text": "So what does this equation tell us?"
        },
        {
          "start": 179.58,
          "end": 188.14,
          "text": "mR, the mass of the rocket, is less later on than it was before,"
        },
        {
          "start": 188.14,
          "end": 194.46,
          "text": "which means this term here is going to be less than 0,"
        },
        {
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 199.74,
          "text": "which means the velocity is our initial velocity minus"
        },
        {
          "start": 199.74,
          "end": 205.66,
          "text": "something, which means we have a decrease in velocity, which"
        },
        {
          "start": 205.66,
          "end": 209.9,
          "text": "means my sled will eventually come to a stop."
        }
